export anchor FolkRosemalingStyle:
    number: 150
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Folk rosemaling
    idea: The dashboard is a painted farmhouse cupboard, with the totals on drawer fronts, each project on a small painted door, and blue frames carrying red and ochre scrolls and flowers in their corners.
    base: light
    palette:
        wallCream: #f3ead8, the page behind the cupboard
        panelCream: #fcf6ea, painted panels and fields
        cupboardBlue: #234a78, the cupboard frame, headings, figures, the current tab, last week bars and the outer focus ring
        skyWash: #dde7f1, progress tracks, the bell and list rows
        folkRed: #a3302a, flowers, the brand, the primary button, the overdue banner, Behind and this week bars
        ochre: #c8892a, inner frame lines, flower centres and the focus outline, never text
        leafGreen: #3c6a37, leaves, progress fills and On track
        drawerWood: #e7d6b6, drawer fronts
        ink: #2a2522, text
        muted: #5e544a, dates and meta
        amber: #7d5100, At risk
    type:
        Brand, greeting and style title use Segoe Script, Apple Chancery,
        Brush Script MT, URW Chancery L, cursive at 34 to 46px. Headings,
        figures, nav and buttons use Bookman Old Style, URW Bookman,
        Cambria, Georgia, serif in bold. Body uses Candara, Segoe UI, Noto
        Sans, Calibri, sans-serif. Drawer figures 54px, panel titles 24px
        centred, door titles 17px, body 15 to 16px at 1.55.
    layout:
        One painted cupboard up to 1240px, a 16px blue frame with round
        top corners and a darker ledge below. The header is a cream crest
        with a wide arched top and a red inner line, holding a tulip and
        the script brand, rounded nav with a blue current pill, a round
        search, a red pill button with a cream inner line, a sky bell and
        a red avatar ringed in ochre. A cream greeting panel with ochre
        inner line and painted C scrolls with tulips in both top corners
        centres the script greeting, date and a red pill naming 4 overdue
        tasks. Four drawer fronts in wood colour each have a red knob on
        the top edge, a large figure, the label and a small red flower.
        Below, a wide panel with corner scrolls holds six painted doors in
        three columns, white with arched tops and blue and red inner
        lines, each with a tulip, the name, category and due date, a green
        vine progress bar ending in a red leaf, the percent, task count
        and status. A narrow column holds the chart, round blue then red
        bars with ochre flame marks on a green ground line, and the
        activity list led by small red and blue leaves. On phones
        everything stacks to one column.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between all panels like boards in one frame, 24 to 28px inside panels.
    density: Medium. Everything sits inside one painted cupboard.
    corners: Soft. 10px panels, wide arched tops on the crest and doors, pills for buttons and banners.
    borders: A 16px blue cupboard frame, ochre inner lines inset 5px in every panel, red inner lines on doors, dotted lines between feed items.
    shadows: Only a solid darker blue ledge under the cupboard.
    icons:
        Painted folk shapes, C scrolls with tulips in panel corners and
        small flowers on drawers. Status uses a heart for On track, a
        diamond with a mark for At risk and a down pointing triangle for
        Behind, beside the word.
    focus: A 3px ochre outline offset 2px inside a 6px blue ring.
    tone: Homely and kind, such as Six doors, one for each piece of work and What the team has been up to.
